sentences.l:
The beloved promised his-union and kept-faith to-me * in a-night I-shall-count-it as-nights;
O a-night time was-generous to-us with-it * in the heedlessness of the slanderers and the blamers!
The beloved spent-the-night clasping-me with his-right-hand, * (and) from my-joy I-clasped-him with my-left;
I-embraced-him and sipped the wine of his-saliva, * and won the honeyed and the honey-gatherers.
